The following termcap entry puts the status line on line 25 of the
Wyse-85 terminal(*).  I call my Wyse85 a "vt200", but the entries won't
work on a real VT220/240 because they take advantage of the extened
command set provided by Wyse- you may have to rename the entries.  This
entry should work fine for practically anything (even any software with
hard-coded 24 line screens!).

Enjoy!

* The Wyse85 is a compatible superset of the dec VT220.  It has 25
  lines, a larger screen, and programmable shifted AND UNSHIFTED FUNCTION
  KEYS!!!  The emulation is pretty darn good, (although control-space
  isn't ^@), and I love the thing (the price is right, too: we paid $525
  ea. for 3)(**).

** Neither my Company nor I are afficliated with Wyse or its
   distibuters. (etc.)

